## Attributions

This project incorporates or is derived from the following open-source projects,
each licensed under the MIT License:

### Understand-Anything
Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Egonex AI
Source: https://github.com/Egonex-AI/Understand-Anything
License: MIT

The Understand-Anything plugin provides AI-powered codebase knowledge graph
analysis. The `/rapidx:understand-anything*` commands in this package are
wrappers around Understand-Anything's skill engine, installed during setup
from the upstream repository.

### Get-Shit-Done (GSD) Workflow Engine
Copyright (c) 2024-2026 gsd-build contributors
Source: https://github.com/gsd-build/get-shit-done
License: MIT

The RapidX workflow engine (plan → build → review → test → ship) is derived
from the GSD workflow engine. All user-facing names have been rebranded to
"RapidX". The underlying vendored engine directory (`get-things-done/`) retains
its original path for compatibility.

### Everything-Claude-Code Enterprise Component Library
Copyright (c) 2024-2026 Affaan M and contributors
Source: https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code
License: MIT

The enterprise component library (rules, skills, agents, hooks, security
patterns, compliance packs, multi-client profiles) is derived from the
everything-claude-code project.
